                <head>315. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Telegram 2404 to Vienna, March 18, authorized Ambassador Matthews to exchange
                    notes with the Austrian Government on settlement of claims under Article 26 of
                    the Austrian State Treaty, which provided for compensation of political
                    persecutees. (Department of State, Central Files, 263.0041–A/3–1359) Delays by
                    the British and French, who concluded similar agreements, postponed the exchange
                    until May 1959. For text of the treaty, which entered into force on May 22, see
                    10 UST 1158.</p>
            </div>
